 ## Overview
-Projection and Ray Geometry defines the mathematical relationship between the 3D volume data and the 2D image plane by establishing the origin, direction, and traversal parameters of the rays used in direct volume ray casting. It solves the problem of mapping pixel coordinates to volumetric space, determining which voxels contribute to which pixels. It is distinguished from sibling methods by its foundational role: while [Standard Ray Casting](12643-standard-ray-casting.md) implements the sampling loop, this family defines the coordinate systems (perspective vs. parallel) and ray generation logic that precede sampling.
